Z||000002||Patrick||01-16-2000||04:25 AM||||<BR>At the Yahoo auction site, there's a section where you can post a question (or in this case, a comment) to the seller about the item being sold. Here's an interesting exchange that's taken place there regarding these scoops.<P><B>tmcoo</B> - They will make the engine run hotter. I happen to know a bit more about airflow than most people.<P><B>byefi</B> - Not true again. Your knowledge of airflow is hindered by your opinion. FACT: The scoupes are installed on my vehicle now. FACT: The car NEVER reaches temperatures above 200 degrees while in motion. FACT: You have NO evidence to prove your theory is correct. FACT: You are PREDICTING that the engine WILL run hotter, which you cannot support. FACT: You are simply WRONG.||||reg||6
Z||000003||TOM||01-16-2000||11:17 AM||||That was me that posted the comment that got him so hot. I may be wrong but being an aircraft mechanic I think I do know abit more about airflow problems that him and than most people. In my line if you have an engine airflow problem you are going to put it down someplace not too pretty and hopefully no one dies.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GWMORGAN||01-16-2000||12:27 PM||||TOM...Please explain why it would it make the engine run hotter.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||01-16-2000||12:38 PM||||I think I can explain this one also. It has something to do with heat having a natural tendency to rise. The rear grills allow cooler air from under the car to rise up through the engine compartment, pick up heat radiated from the engine and rise through the grills. The design of the rear window area creates a low pressure area while the vheicle is in motion. This causes heat to be sucked out from the engine compartment. That guys weird scoops force air down into the engine compartment, offsetting the natural cooling effect of the rising heat. There will be a speed where a balance between the incoming air and the rising heat will be cancelled, causing no air flow over then engine. This is the speed where overheating of stuff in the engine compartment will occur. There, does that make sense to everyone? Welcome to Cooter's second grade Fiero classroom!.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||01-16-2000||01:15 PM||||Let me pose a solution/question.  I know a little about aerodynamics but nothing about air flow.  What if someone installed one of Toms' hood scoops?  Wouldn't that let the hot air out as the other scoops sucked air in?  IMHO, it would look too cluttered, but I'm just trying to find a hypothetical solution.  I'll bet this would work.  Maybe if you installed some kind of air filtration system in the over the roof scoops then made some kind of tubes (or whatever) directly to the intake?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gokart||01-16-2000||03:06 PM||||I'm POSITIVE your car will over heat with those scoops CAUSE I HAD THEM!! When I get my scanner working I'll post pictures of my first Fiero, they did look sharp. I had to pull the thermostat in the summer cause of Cape traffic, something I would NEVER do now cause I didn't know any better back then.||||reg||4
